            <ArticleTitle>[Effect of emotional-pain stress on the adrenocholinoreactivity of the smooth muscle of the portal vein].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>5-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Effect of emotional painful stress (EPS) on adreno- and cholinoreactivity of the portal vein was studied. EPS produced a significant decrease in adrenoceptor sensitivity of the vein to noradrenaline, which was not accompanied by a significant change of cholinoceptor sensitivity to acetylcholine. A possible mechanism of the phenomenon is discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
